// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO1-4/6/7/21/35-42 - dedicated onboard SD
// card SPI bus, I2S mic, I2S amp, RTC interrupt, and RGB LED power gate
// (see vendor pins_arduino.h). Buttons, VBAT/VBUS sense, and RGB_DATA
// LED are kept.
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO18 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard
// RGB_DATA driving the 40x8 (320 LED) addressable RGB matrix
// (github.com/UnexpectedMaker/arduino-esp32 variants/um_bling/pins_arduino.h;
// help.unexpectedmaker.com "What is BLING!?").
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO11 and GPIO10 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard
// user buttons BUTTON_A/BUTTON_B of BLING!'s 4 user-programmable
// buttons (github.com/UnexpectedMaker/arduino-esp32
// variants/um_bling/pins_arduino.h; help.unexpectedmaker.com "What is
// BLING!?"). BUTTON_C (GPIO33) and BUTTON_D (GPIO34) NOT tagged - those
// GPIOs fall in the chip-level octal-flash/PSRAM exclusion range
// (GPIO33-37) already removed from chipGpios; see notes.txt.
